# Save before worldserver restart

Default is **hold live**. Do not start this sequence unless the user explicitly asked to ship, restart, deploy, or replace worldserver. See `hold-live-until-ship.mdc`.

When they have asked: before any action that reboots or replaces `ac-worldserver` (`docker compose build` + `up`, `restart`, `kill`), run `powershell tools/restart_worldserver.ps1`. Skip only if the container is not running. Players otherwise take sizeable rollbacks.

That script announces in-game (`announce` + `notify`), waits **45 seconds**, then `saveall`. After it prints OK, docker compose replace is allowed. Do not use AzerothCore `server shutdown` for a docker replace (that stops the process on its own timer and races saveall).

Prefer SOAP on port 7878 when it is live. Never print SOAP passwords. Do not pipe to `docker attach` (non-TTY stdin is rejected; EOF can shut the server down). Immediate `saveall` without a warning: `powershell tools/save_world.ps1`.
